kernel.sysctl
  Harden kernel settings
  Does not apply to this host: kernel settings belong to the host inside a
  container.

Why
  Hides kernel addresses and logs from normal users, restricts BPF, ptrace and
  perf, protects shared directories such as /tmp, and turns on SYN cookies.

Params (in the module's profile table)
  none

Fixes these audit controls
  KRN-001 [low] Kernel pointers hidden
  KRN-002 [low] Kernel log restricted to root
  KRN-003 [medium] Unprivileged BPF disabled
  KRN-004 [medium] ptrace scope restricted
  KRN-005 [medium] Symlink protection enabled
  KRN-006 [medium] Hardlink protection enabled
  KRN-007 [low] FIFO protection enabled
  KRN-008 [low] Regular file protection enabled
  KRN-009 [low] Setuid core dumps restricted
  KRN-010 [medium] Address space randomization fully enabled
  KRN-011 [low] Kernel profiling restricted
  NET-001 [low] TCP SYN cookies enabled
  NET-002 [low] Source-routed packets rejected
  NET-003 [low] Broadcast pings ignored
